LUTAR-1#1 Warning
LUT drives async reset alert  
LUT cell u_video_timing/i_wrap_i_1, with 2 or more inputs, drives asynchronous preset/clear pin(s) u_hdmi_tx/i_wrap/TMDS_0/i_ODDRE_N/RST,
u_hdmi_tx/i_wrap/TMDS_0/i_ODDRE_P/RST,
u_hdmi_tx/i_wrap/TMDS_1/i_ODDRE_N/RST,
u_hdmi_tx/i_wrap/TMDS_1/i_ODDRE_P/RST,
u_hdmi_tx/i_wrap/TMDS_2/i_ODDRE_N/RST,
u_hdmi_tx/i_wrap/TMDS_2/i_ODDRE_P/RST,
u_hdmi_tx/i_wrap/TMDS_3/i_ODDRE_N/RST
u_hdmi_tx/i_wrap/TMDS_3/i_ODDRE_P/RST. The LUT may glitch and trigger an unexpected reset, even if it is a properly timed path.
Related violations: <none>

CLKC-24#1 Advisory
MMCME4 with ZHOLD drives sequential IO not with CLKOUT0  
The MMCME4 cell u_clk_wiz_0/inst/mmcme4_adv_inst has COMPENSATION value ZHOLD, but CLKOUT1 output drives sequential IO cells. In order to achieve insertion delay and phase-alignment for the IO sequential cells, CLKOUT0 must be used.
Related violations: <none>


